        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: C.R.A.Z.Y.\n- People: Jean-Marc Vallée, François Boulay, Patsy Cline, Randy Hughes\n- Music: Pink Floyd, The Rolling Stones\n- Topics: film soundtrack, country music, plane crash\n\nFacts:\n- Patsy Cline, born Virginia Patterson Hensley, was born on September 8, 1932 and was an American country music singer.\n- Patsy Cline died at age 30 on March 5, 1963 in a multiple-fatality crash involving the private plane of her manager, Randy Hughes.\n- C.R.A.Z.Y. is a 2005 French-language Canadian coming-of-age drama film directed by Jean-Marc Vallée and co-written by Jean-Marc Vallée and François Boulay.\n- C.R.A.Z.Y. uses an extensive soundtrack that includes music by Pink Floyd, Patsy Cline, and The Rolling Stones.",
